This project has a code knowledge graph at graphify-out/. See
`docs/AI_TOOLING.md` for the full cross-IDE setup.

**Prefer orienting with the graph before exploring with Read/Grep/Glob/Bash.**
This is a preference, **not a hard gate** — if no graph tool is available, just
use normal exploration. In order of preference:
1. **CodeGraphContext MCP** (preferred; portable, works in every IDE; wired in
   `.cursor/mcp.json`) — find callers, dependencies, definitions.
2. **`graphify` CLI** — `graphify query "<question>"`, `graphify path "<A>" "<B>"`,
   `graphify explain "<concept>"`. Only if installed locally (private pip package;
   absent in CI, fresh clones, and non-Windows machines).
3. **Read the data directly** — `graphify-out/graph.json`, or
   `graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md` for broad architecture review.

Use Read/Grep/Glob directly to modify or debug specific lines, when the graph
lacks needed detail, or when no graph tool is present. After changing code,
refresh via the CodeGraphContext indexer (or `graphify update .` if installed).
